From 42b81c973eba0a00b17e0e63179631f692afd30b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 04:36:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] docs: use zapp2 instead of the obsolete applicative2'

applicative2' was renamed to zapp2 in 1.9.1 and is marked ObsoleteAttribute. Because that
attribute is declared with isError=false the old spelling still compiles with only a warning,
so this use survived the rename unnoticed.

This is the only obsolete computation expression spelling remaining anywhere under
docsrc/content.
---
 docsrc/content/abstraction-zipapplicative.fsx | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/docsrc/content/abstraction-zipapplicative.fsx b/docsrc/content/abstraction-zipapplicative.fsx
index c4fbed3..ba13555 100644
--- a/docsrc/content/abstraction-zipapplicative.fsx
+++ b/docsrc/content/abstraction-zipapplicative.fsx
@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@ open FSharpPlus
 
 // Validations
 
-let validated = applicative2' {
+let validated = zapp2 {
     let! x = async { return Ok 1 }
     and! y = async { return Error ["Error1"] }
     and! z = async { return Error ["Error2"] }
